Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the Next.js project.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` version 2.0.1
- Updated package.json and package-lock.json with the new dependency

### 2. Analytics Configuration
Modified `app/layout.tsx`:
- Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next"`
- Added `<Analytics />` component inside the body element, after the children prop
- This ensures analytics tracking is enabled across all pages of the application

### 3. Verification
- Build completed successfully with no errors
- TypeScript compilation passed
- All routes generated correctly (20 pages total)
- Pre-existing linting issues are unrelated to these changes

## Implementation Details

The implementation follows the official Vercel Analytics documentation (fetched from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart):
- Used the Next.js App Router specific package: `@vercel/analytics/next`
- Placed the Analytics component in the root layout to ensure site-wide tracking
- Positioned the component after the children to follow best practices for loading order

## Next Steps

Once deployed to Vercel, the analytics will automatically begin collecting data:
- Page views
- Visitor metrics
- Performance data

No additional configuration is required. The analytics will be visible in the Vercel dashboard after deployment.
